igital point, pump running status (read from PLC)\n   - `PUMP_CMD` - Digital point, pump start/stop command (write to PLC)\n   - `PUMP_SPEED` - Analog point, pump speed/frequency (0-100%)\n   - `FLOW` - Analog point, flow rate\n   - `PRESSURE` - Analog point, inlet/outlet pressure\n   - `LEVEL` - Analog point, water level\n   - `PUMP_FAULT` - Digital point, pump fault status\n\n2. **HMI Page:**\n   - Main pump station control page\n   - Pump widget showing status\n   - Start/Stop buttons (bound to PUMP_CMD)\n   - Indicators for running status and fault\n   - Displays for analog values (flow, pressure, level)\n\n3. **Alarms:**\n   - High pressure alarm\n   - Low pressure alarm\n   - High level alarm\n   - Pump fault alarm (digital)\n\nI'm going to start by creating all the necessary points first."}, {"turn": 3, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 4753, "output_tokens": 623, "latency_ms": 13336.741000006441, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "参数有误，让我修正后重新创建：", "reasoning": "I see the issue - the schema uses \"type\" as a required field (not \"data_type\"), and for boolean points min/max should be null or 0. Let me fix the calls. I need to use \"type\" instead of \"data_type\", and for bool points min/max should be omitted or set to null."}, {"turn": 4, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 5707, "output_tokens": 605, "latency_ms": 14675.994399993215, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "看起来批量调用有问题，让我逐个创建点位：", "reasoning": "Hmm, still getting errors. The first one succeeded but the rest failed. Let me look at the schema more carefully. The create_point action has these properties:\n- action (required)\n- tag (required)\n- type (required) - but I'm providing \"type\"...\n\nWait, maybe the parameter name is different. Let me check - the schema shows `\"data_type\"` in my first attempt and `\"type\"` in my second. But the error says \"create_point.type: Field required\" which means the system expects a field called \"type\" but I'm sending \"data_type\" or vice versa.\n\nActually looking at the error message more carefully: \"create_point.type: Field required\" - this means the \"type\" field IS required and it's not being found. But I'm sending \"type\": \"bool\"... \n\nWait, the first call succeeded. Let me check what's different. The first call had:\n- action: create_point\n- tag: PUMP_CMD\n- type: bool\n- description: 泵启停控制命令\n- mode: rw\n\nBut the second call had the same structure plus min/max. The error for the second call says \"create_point.min: Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\" - but I didn't provide min/max for bool points. And \"create_point.type: Field required\" - but I did provide type...\n\nOh wait, I think the issue is that the schema has `data_type` as the field name, not `type`. Let me look at the schema definition again...\n\nThe schema properties are: action, tag, type, unit, description, min, max, mode\n\nBut the error says \"type: Field required\" - this is confusing because I AM providing it. \n\nActually, looking at the first result - it returned ok:true but count:0 and points:[]. Maybe the first one succeeded but the response format is just showing the current points list?\n\nLet me try again with \"data_type\" as the parameter name since that's what the original schema showed... wait no, the schema clearly shows \"type\" as a property.\n\nLet me try a different approach - maybe the issue is that for bool points, I should not pass min/max at all, and for float points I need to pass numeric values. Let me also try passing min and max as numbers for the analog points.\n\nActually, I wonder if the issue is with the second point. The error message seems to be about the second call having issues. Let me try creating them one at a time to isolate the issue."}, {"turn": 5, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 6349, "output_tokens": 102, "latency_ms": 2625.02969999332, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "OK so that worked. Let me continue with the rest one by one. The bool points should work without min/max. For float points, I need to provide min and max as numbers."}, {"turn": 6, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 6488, "output_tokens": 101, "latency_ms": 3498.497500026133, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "Good, let me continue with the float points."}, {"turn": 7, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 6626, "output_tokens": 99, "latency_ms": 3972.8771000518464, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "Good, continuing with the rest."}, {"turn": 8, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 6762, "output_tokens": 97, "latency_ms": 2463.1414999603294, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "Good, continuing."}, {"turn": 9, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 6896, "output_tokens": 99, "latency_ms": 4714.189900027122, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "Good, one more point to create."}, {"turn": 10, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 7032, "output_tokens": 177, "latency_ms": 4298.593400046229, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "✅ 7个点位全部创建完成！\n\n---\n\n## 🖥️ 第二步：创建泵站控制台 HMI 页面", "reasoning": "All points created. Now let me create the HMI page and widgets. I need to:\n1. Create a main pump station control page\n2. Add widgets: pump indicator, start/stop button, speed display, flow display, pressure display, tank level, fault indicator\n3. Bind points to widgets\n\nLet me create the page first."}, {"turn": 11, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 7246, "output_tokens": 458, "latency_ms": 8223.767600022256, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "现在添加控件到页面上：", "reasoning": "Page created. Now let me add widgets to the page. I need to create various widgets for the pump station control console. Let me plan the layout:\n\n- Top area: Title\n- Left side: Pump visualization (tank, pump)\n- Center: Control panel (start/stop buttons, indicators)\n- Right side: Analog displays (flow, pressure, level, speed)\n\nLet me create the widgets. I'll use different widget types:\n- tank: for the water tank\n- pump: for the pump\n- button: for start/stop\n- indicator: for status\n- gauge: for analog values\n- text: for labels\n\nLet me create them."}, {"turn": 12, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 7770, "output_tokens": 351, "latency_ms": 8340.95449995948, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "Good, widgets are being created. Let me continue with the control buttons and indicators."}], "rag": {"enabled": true, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 12, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker": true}, "workflow": {"enabled": true, "selected_workflow": "AlarmConfig"}, "totals": {"input_tokens": 70081, "output_tokens": 3853, "cost_usd": 0.0, "e2e_latency_ms": 90017.44429999962}, "judge": null}
