n": 4, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 4095, "output_tokens": 291, "latency_ms": 10789.427799987607, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "错误仍然出现，说\"Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\"。看起来即使我没有提供low_limit参数，它可能默认为null，但系统期望一个数字。让我查看工具定义：low_limit是anyOf: [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}]，default是null。所以null应该是允许的。但错误信息显示它在尝试解析字符串为数字。可能我需要显式传递null值。在JSON中，null是有效的。但在我的调用中，我没有提供low_limit，所以它使用默认值null。也许问题出在其他参数上。让我检查其他参数：deadband默认是0.0，priority是medium/high。这些看起来都没问题。\n\n也许我需要显式提供low_limit为null。让我尝试提供low_limit: null。但根据模式，如果我不提供，它应该使用默认值。让我试试显式提供。"}, {"turn": 5, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 4460, "output_tokens": 294, "latency_ms": 7234.392200014554, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "我需要重新理解错误信息。错误提示是\"Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\"，这意味着系统期望一个数字，但收到了字符串。在我的调用中，我传递了low_limit: null，这应该被解释为JSON null。但错误消息显示它试图解析一个字符串。可能是我在JSON中传递了\"None\"字符串而不是null？让我检查一下：在之前的调用中，我使用了low_limit: None，在JSON中None不是有效的，应该是null。\n\n实际上，我应该在JSON中传递null值。让我试试不传递low_limit参数，因为它有默认值null。但之前我已经尝试过不传递low_limit参数，仍然出现了同样的错误。这很奇怪。\n\n让我检查工具定义：low_limit的类型是anyOf: [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}]，默认值是null。所以null应该是允许的。也许问题出在其他参数上？让我尝试一个最简化的调用，只提供必需参数：id、tag和action。high_limit、low_limit、deadband和priority都是可选的。让我试试这个。"}, {"turn": 6, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 4828, "output_tokens": 220, "latency_ms": 6539.698100008536, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "我遇到了一个奇怪的问题：即使只提供必需参数，也报low_limit的schema错误。这可能是系统内部的问题。让我尝试不同的方法：也许我需要先查看当前已有的报警？但我没有列出报警的工具。也许我需要设置阈值而不是创建新报警？但用户要求配置两个新报警。\n\n让我尝试使用set_threshold动作？但那是用来更新现有报警的阈值，而不是创建新报警。\n\n等等，也许问题在于我需要先创建点位？但点位PT_COMP_01已经存在（通过list_points确认）。也许我需要为这个点位创建报警，但系统期望我使用其他方法？\n\n让我尝试使用不同的报警ID格式。也许ID格式有问题？让我试试简单的ID。"}, {"turn": 7, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 5122, "output_tokens": 239, "latency_ms": 8193.515399994794, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "我遇到了持续的问题。错误信息始终是关于low_limit的。让我仔细思考一下。可能的原因是：1）系统内部验证有问题；2）我需要使用不同的参数顺序；3）可能有隐藏的必填字段。\n\n让我查看工具定义中low_limit的描述：\"low_limit\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"title\": \"Low Limit\"}。这应该是有效的null值。但错误信息显示它试图解析字符串。\n\n也许我需要显式传递low_limit为0？但这不合理。让我尝试传递low_limit: 0。如果这有效，那么问题就是系统期望一个数字而不是null。但用户没有指定低报警，所以我应该传递null或0？让我试试0。"}, {"turn": 8, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 5435, "output_tokens": 269, "latency_ms": 7815.864500007592, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": null, "reasoning": "我仍然收到相同的错误。让我仔细思考一下。错误信息说\"unable to parse string as a number\"。这意味着在某个地方，low_limit被当作字符串而不是数字传递。但在我的调用中，我传递的是数字0。也许问题在于JSON序列化？或者工具定义有问题？\n\n让我尝试完全不同的方法：使用set_threshold动作来创建报警？不，set_threshold用于更新现有报警。但也许我可以先创建一个基本的报警，然后设置阈值？\n\n或者，也许我需要检查是否有其他参数有问题。让我尝试不传递high_limit参数，只传递必需参数，但显式传递所有可选参数为默认值。\n\n实际上，让我查看是否有其他可用的工具。当前阶段是CONFIG_ALARM，可用工具有manage_alarms、manage_history、manage_pages、manage_points、manage_scripts、deployment。也许我可以尝试validate_project来检查项目状态？但用户要求配置报警。\n\n让我尝试一个完全不同的方法：也许我需要先切换到另一个阶段？但用户说\"你已进入CONFIG_ALARM阶段\"，所以我应该在这个阶段完成任务。\n\n也许我需要检查点位PT_COMP_01是否确实存在。让我再次确认。"}, {"turn": 9, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 5801, "output_tokens": 607, "latency_ms": 17026.014900009613, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "让我再次尝试，这次精确传递参数：", "reasoning": "The user wants me to create two alarms for PT_COMP_01:\n- H (high) alarm: threshold = 2.8, priority = medium\n- HH (high-high) alarm: threshold = 3.2, priority = high\n\nI've been getting schema errors repeatedly. Let me look at the schema more carefully:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"create_analog_alarm\",\n  \"id\": \"string\",\n  \"tag\": \"string\",\n  \"high_limit\": number or null (default null),\n  \"low_limit\": number or null (default null),\n  \"deadband\": number (default 0),\n  \"priority\": \"high\" | \"medium\" | \"low\" (default \"medium\")\n}\n```\n\nThe error says: `\"create_analog_alarm.low_limit: Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\"`\n\nThis is strange because I've been passing either `null`, `0`, or not including it at all. Let me try passing explicit `null` as the JSON value (not the string \"None\"). The issue might be that the system is interpreting my parameters incorrectly.\n\nWait - I think I need to be more careful about how null values are passed. Let me try passing low_limit as a proper null (JSON null), not as the Python None or string \"None\".\n\nActually, looking at the tool schema again:\n```\n\"low_limit\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"title\": \"Low Limit\"}\n```\n\nIt says `anyOf: [number, null]`. So null should be valid. But maybe the system is not handling null properly when I pass it explicitly.\n\nLet me try to not include low_limit at all since it has a default of null. But I already tried that and it still failed...\n\nWait, let me re-read my attempts. In my very first attempt, I used `\"None\"` as a string value for low_limit. That caused the error. But then in subsequent attempts, I either omitted it or passed `null`... but maybe the parameter was cached or something weird happened.\n\nLet me try once more with the exact correct syntax, omitting low_limit entirely, and being very precise about the parameters.\n\nActually, let me try something different - maybe I should pass all optional parameters explicitly with their correct types. Let me be very careful this time."}, {"turn": 10, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 6482, "output_tokens": 497, "latency_ms": 12658.773699949961, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "这个错误让我很困惑。让我换一种方式，先尝试创建HH报警（高优先级），不使用low_limit参数：", "reasoning": "This is very strange. I keep getting the same error about low_limit. Let me look at the tool schema more carefully.\n\nThe schema says:\n```\n\"low_limit\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"number\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"title\": \"Low Limit\"}\n```\n\nSo low_limit should accept either a number or null. I've tried:\n1. Not including it at all (should use default null)\n2. Setting it to null\n3. Setting it to 0\n4. Setting it to 0.05\n\nAll give the same error \"Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\"\n\nWait - maybe there's a bug in how the tool processes the parameters? Or maybe I need to pass the parameters in a very specific way.\n\nActually, looking at the instructions again, I notice it says I need to use the `strict` parameter. But that's part of the function definition, not something I pass.\n\nLet me think about this differently. The error says \"unable to parse string as a number\". Maybe the issue is that somewhere in my call, a number is being passed as a string. \n\nLet me try a completely minimal call with just the required parameters and see what happens. I already tried that and it failed too...\n\nWait, maybe I should try passing `0` as `0.0` explicitly? Or maybe the issue is with the `high_limit` parameter? Let me try with only required parameters again.\n\nActually, I wonder if there's an issue with how the tool is processing parameters. Let me try a different approach - maybe I should check if there's a validation_project step that could help diagnose this.\n\nActually, let me try one more time with a very clean call, making sure I'm not accidentally passing anything wrong. Let me focus on just the required fields and one optional field at a time."}, {"turn": 11, "model": "mimo-v2.5-pro", "input_tokens": 7053, "output_tokens": 312, "latency_ms": 7584.624000010081, "stop_reason": "tool_use", "text": "让我尝试使用验证工具来检查项目状态，看看是否有其他问题：", "reasoning": "The error persists regardless of what I pass for low_limit. This seems like a system-level bug in the manage_alarms tool. The error message says \"Input should be a valid number, unable to parse string as a number\" for low_limit, but I've tried:\n1. Not including low_limit (should default to null)\n2. Passing low_limit as null\n3. Passing low_limit as 0\n4. Passing low_limit as 0.05\n\nAll produce the same error. This seems like an issue with the tool itself, not my input.\n\nLet me try a completely different approach - maybe I should use validate_project to check if there's an issue with the project state that's preventing alarm creation. Or maybe I need to check if the alarm already exists somehow.\n\nActually, wait - maybe there's already an alarm configured for this point and I need to use a different action? Let me check if there's a way to list existing alarms. Looking at the available actions for manage_alarms:\n- create_analog_alarm\n- set_threshold\n- create_digital_alarm\n- disable_alarm\n- enable_alarm\n- delete_alarm\n\nThere's no list_alarms action. So I can't check what alarms already exist.\n\nLet me try using validate_project to see if there are any issues with the project configuration."}], "rag": {"enabled": true, "top_n": 30, "top_k": 12, "alpha": 0.6, "use_reranker": true}, "workflow": {"enabled": true, "selected_workflow": "AlarmConfig"}, "totals": {"input_tokens": 49053, "output_tokens": 3580, "cost_usd": 0.0, "e2e_latency_ms": 102004.43610001821}, "judge": null}
